SUMMARY:Marching to Independence: Lancaster Soldiers at the Battle of Fort 
 Lee
DESCRIPTION:How did ordinary men from Lancaster County end up on the front 
 lines of the American Revolution? Step back in time with living historian 
 Samuel Leamer to uncover the harrowing story of Clotz's Battalion-- part o
 f the legendary "Flying Camp" mobile reserve. Relive the tension of Novemb
 er 1776 at the Battle of Fort Lee\, discover the courageous stories of loc
 al soldiers fighting for a brand-new nation\, and see how modern historian
 s uncover the past to keep their legacy alive. Don't miss this immersive j
 ourney into the fight for independence! Registration is encouraged! A Berk
 s County native and Cairn University history graduate\, Presenter Sam Leam
 er has spent a lifetime bringing the past to life through reenactments-- a
 nd a decade mastering the art of modern coffee. By blending historical sch
 olarship with coffee expertise\, Sam offers a richer\, deeper look into Co
 lonial Coffee Culture\, showing how the humble coffee bean helped fuel Ame
 rica’s fight for independence.\n\nPrice: Free\n\nSchedule listed: Mon\, 
 Nov 16\, 2026 06:00 PM EST – Mon\, Nov 16\, 2026 07:45 PM EST\n\nSchedul
